     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/attach/803ee929bf523/eeeee.JPG?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"eeeee.JPG\" width=\"459\" height=\"166\"><br><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Dear Phil,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I fit four models to the operational\r\ndata of an English language proficiency test using both R package <i>mirt</i>\r\nand <i>BMIRT Toolkit</i> (Yao,2003, 2013<a style=\"color:blue\" href=\"#m_-8293169578119720113__ftn1\" name=\"m_-8293169578119720113__ftnref1\" title=\"\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"vertical-align:super\"><span style=\"vertical-align:super\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">[1]</span></span></span></a>).\r\nThe models include unidimensional IRT, uncorrelated factor multidimensional\r\nIRT, correlated factor multidimensional IRT, and bifactor. Surprisingly, the\r\nAIC and BIC values obtained from the two programs were different (please see\r\nTable 2 in the attachments). While, based on <i>mirt</i>, bifactor model\r\nhad the best and uncorrelated MIRT had the worst fit, in <i>BMIRT</i>\r\nunidimensional model had the best and bifactor model had the worst fit.\r\nConsidering that I rechecked the steps in doing the analyses and ran the\r\nanalyses several times to make sure I haven’t made a mistake, how can this\r\ndifference be explained?</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I’d be grateful if you could help me\r\nwith this.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Best regards,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Mohammad</span></p>\r\n\r\n<div><br clear=\"all\">\r\n\r\n<hr align=\"left\" size=\"1\" width=\"33%\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt 14.2pt;text-align:justify;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><a style=\"color:blue\" href=\"#m_-8293169578119720113__ftnref1\" name=\"m_-8293169578119720113__ftn1\" title=\"\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"vertical-align:super\"><span style=\"vertical-align:super\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:107%\">[1]</span></span></span></a>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Yao, L. (2003). BMIRT: Bayesian multivariate item response theory\r\n[computer software]. Monterey, CA: Defense Manpower Data Center. Downloaded\r\nfrom </span><a href=\"https://www.bmirt.com/6271.html\" style=\"color:blue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.bmirt.com/6271.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471545581000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OCEk8z6vLdQKONcjs06nz\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">https://www.bmirt.com/6271.html</span></a><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt 14.2pt;text-align:justify;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Yao, L. (2013). The BMIRT toolkit. Monterey. </span><a href=\"https://www.bmirt.com/8220.html\" style=\"color:blue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.bmirt.com/8220.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471545581000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2x6rsaYmjZhMu5GsJfB9W8\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">https://www.bmirt.com/8220.html</span></a><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div></div>\r\n"
